OL,3,GNEWSAFarmer feels 'helpless' after
OL,4,Abluetongue outbreak
OL,5,
OL,6,FA farmer said she felt "helpless" and
OL,7,Fconsidered selling up her farm after
OL,8,Fher entire herd of cattle was infected
OL,9,Fwith the bluetongue virus (BVT).
OL,11,FSally Phillips, co-owner of Burleaze
OL,12,FFarm in Ilminster, Somerset, said the
OL,13,Fdisease, which causes illness in cattle
OL,14,Fand is commonly fatal to sheep,
OL,15,Fseverely limited milk production at her
OL,16,Ffarm, costing around #11,000.
OL,18,FIt comes after 350 farms in Somerset,
OL,19,F28 in Wiltshire, 18 in Gloucestershire
OL,20,Fand one in Bristol declared confirmed
OL,21,Fcases of the virus since July.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,349,340,200,160,0,100
